{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/messages/openai.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T21:02:47.407678Z","id":"da637dbd3c4c69eac753a399b26ad6b8272a3c1cbc605cdef6d184864f1762b8","body":{"detail":"Mistral's chat completions request schema (https://docs.mistral.ai/api/endpoint/chat) lists no stream_options, and an unknown field is refused there, so body() leaves it out for api.mistral.ai. The same page does not say whether the final chunk carries usage. If it does not, Translator::end_message (openai.rs:466-471) fails every Mistral turn with Protocol \"the stream carried no token usage\". The host table is matched on the base URL's host, so a proxy in front of Mistral gets stream_options and may be refused.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":30},"end":{"line":34},"content_hash":"f9faf1a3c1274e0a1b75bcdf93b3b698ac10922dfb9f9edea469daf7586cc7b8"},"suggested_fix":"Run one ClaxBot turn against https://api.mistral.ai/v1 with zai-glm-5-3-flash and check the last chunk; drop the host table if Mistral accepts stream_options.","summary":"Mistral is assumed to send token usage in its last streamed chunk unasked; no test reaches the real API","tags":["providers","needs-live-check","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/messages/openai.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T21:02:47.407758Z","id":"05325e4da9171481ea6f99ca4f2fc8a29090654ebb88d0519c389074372031a0","body":{"detail":"https://docs.subconscious.dev/api-reference/openapi.json gives POST /chat/completions no tools, tool_choice or tool_calls fields and puts reasoning in <think> tags (handled by ThinkTags here). Its integration pages configure agent tools against https://api.subconscious.dev/v1 with model subconscious/glm-5.3-marathon, which suggests tools work, but nothing here has run a turn there. Its Anthropic-compatible POST /messages documents tools, yet requires thinking {type: enabled, budget_tokens} and has no cache_control, while ClaxBot sends adaptive thinking and cache breakpoints (crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs turn request).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":22},"content_hash":"ed1de8dacf5e1d995c9e38884a7a574108bfb60e9a0fe0c5b81177758299e228"},"summary":"Subconscious's Chat Completions documents no tools or tool_calls; ClaxBot cannot work there unless the endpoint accepts them anyway","tags":["providers","needs-live-check","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/messages/openai.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T21:02:47.407795Z","id":"7b3ec9320b2e4e35e540f18f0d05f20b0efa89807d36a96eee8fd9f75f4735b1","body":{"detail":"Not taken: Subconscious's /messages refuses ClaxBot's adaptive thinking and output_config.effort as documented, so the Messages path would need a per-host request dialect. Chat Completions needs no dialect if its undocumented tool support holds.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":22},"content_hash":"ed1de8dacf5e1d995c9e38884a7a574108bfb60e9a0fe0c5b81177758299e228"},"summary":"Serve Subconscious through api = anthropic at https://api.subconscious.dev instead of Chat Completions","tags":["providers","revisit:a ClaxBot turn on Subconscious Chat Completions fails for want of tool calls","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/messages/openai.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T21:46:41.244374Z","id":"8e4c65fd04ef0c0928d7eb6167b8e7469840480c1a55822749262375acafbe59","body":{"detail":"Failure: an OpenRouter response with usage.is_byok = true and usage.cost = 0 (a BYOK call inside the free allowance) yields billed_micro_usd = Some(0); a run loop that scales the turn's token rows to the billed cost charges nothing. Above the allowance cost is the 5 % fee only. OpenRouter documents usage.cost as \"the total amount charged to your account\" in credits (USD base currency, openrouter.ai/docs/faq) and cost_details.upstream_inference_cost as the upstream provider's charge (openrouter.ai/docs/use-cases/usage-accounting). The translator reads cost alone and ignores is_byok.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":425},"end":{"line":441},"content_hash":"686362b0d9270ac043a5dcd5273dcd32b9578c824091d201f9eb6c188928d897"},"suggested_fix":"When u[\"is_byok\"] is true, set billed_micro_usd to cost + cost_details.upstream_inference_cost when the latter is a finite non-negative number, else leave it None (fall back to resolved rates); add an is_byok case to a_usage_cost_is_the_billed_cost_in_micro_usd.","summary":"A BYOK OpenRouter call's usage.cost is only OpenRouter's fee (often 0), not what the call cost","tags":["pricing","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/messages/openai.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T21:46:41.244464Z","id":"fabc71849b00bcd0ff92454ac25f2222c74540de6afa96ff713abee373a7d550","body":{"detail":"billed_micro_usd rounds to nearest, so usage.cost = 0.0000004 (a short call on a cheap model) becomes Some(0). Scaling a turn's rows to a billed cost of 0 charges cost 0 although the provider billed something. Magnitude per call is below $0.0000005, but the meaning (provider says free) is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":59},"end":{"line":65},"content_hash":"4757436b38eee0680895b2e897639634ecc7720fe324e99aea817ea2d46f81e1"},"suggested_fix":"Round up: (dollars * 1_000_000.0).ceil() as u64, so only a reported 0 is Some(0); update the 0.0012345 case and add a 0.0000004 -> 1 case.","summary":"A nonzero cost under half a micro-USD rounds to Some(0), indistinguishable from a free call","tags":["pricing","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/messages/openai.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T21:49:22.116211Z","id":"c6d493aea9e32826560393329050b7408926fc36f54ebda6fbe7b0f575ab151f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d1c89e455","summary":"billed_micro_usd adds cost_details.upstream_inference_cost to cost when is_byok is true and is None when it is missing, null or negative; messages::tests::wire::a_usage_cost_is_the_billed_cost_in_micro_usd_rounded_up passes (bazel test //crates/clax-sample/... passed (88 passed; 0 failed))","supersedes":"8e4c65fd04ef0c0928d7eb6167b8e7469840480c1a55822749262375acafbe59","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/messages/openai.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T21:49:22.181674Z","id":"df9e430a179453728a5d49525039dcf9f01d5602c17ece0b53d56dec57a16c3e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d1c89e455","summary":"micro_usd_up rounds up (0.0000004 -> 1, 0.000003 -> 3 despite float error); a_usage_cost_is_the_billed_cost_in_micro_usd_rounded_up passes (bazel test //crates/clax-sample/... passed (88 passed; 0 failed))","supersedes":"fabc71849b00bcd0ff92454ac25f2222c74540de6afa96ff713abee373a7d550","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/messages/openai.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T21:50:51.490080Z","id":"8cfae2c107bec63fb33a36a1f2eddd317285865f9628f452b0a3d2a36e9b2caa","body":{"detail":"micro_usd_up (openai.rs:73-84): for dollars = 1e-13, micro = 1e-7, near = 0 and |micro - near| < 1e-6, so it returns 0 although the cost is nonzero; the doc comment's \"rounded up so that only zero is 0\" does not hold. No real bill is that small, so only the contract is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":73},"end":{"line":84},"content_hash":"94f943d1a9aa5ad25705eb329dc113fd34052e8a5b6cd78539641c7b9c1d6a3d"},"suggested_fix":"Either state the contract as \"rounded up, except that a product within 10^-6 of a whole number is that number\" (dropping \"only zero is 0\"), or apply the snap only when near > 0.","summary":"micro_usd_up's doc says only zero is 0, but its 10^-6 guard rounds any cost under 10^-12 USD to 0","tags":["style","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
